 Center — v1.1.2 · QuranEnc.com</span></section><p class=\"cr\">The words of the two imams are given in their original Arabic, verbatim, with references.</p><section><h2>Shaykh al-Islam Ibn Taymiyyah</h2><blockquote class=\"ar\" lang=\"ar\">أي كبر ممقوتا أي كبر مقته مقتا<cite>«الاستقامة» 1/18</cite></blockquote></section><a class=\"btn pri open\" href=\"/tafsir.html?lang=en#s61a3\">Open in the interactive tafsir (full texts)</a><div class=\"pn\"><span></span><a href=\"/en/ayah/61-5.html\">Next verse (61:5)</a></div></main><footer class=\"site-foot\"><span>Tafsir al-Shaykhayn · <a href=\"/en/\">Home</a> · <a href=\"/about.html\">About the project</a> · <a href=\"/privacy.html\">Privacy &amp; terms</a></span><a href=\"https://doersadv.com\" rel=\"noopener\" dir=\"ltr\">Developed by Doers</a></footer>\n</body>\n</html>\n","ayah/61-5.html":"<!doctype html>\n<html lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\">\n<head>\n<meta charset=\"utf-8\">\n<meta name=\"viewport\" content=\"width=device-width, initial-scale=1\">\n<title>Tafsir of As-Saff 61:5 — by Ibn Taymiyyah and Ibn al-Qayyim</title>\n<meta name=\"description\" content=\"And [mention, O Muḥammad], when Moses said to his people, &quot;O my people, why do you harm me while you certainly know that I am the messenger of Allāh to you\">\n<link rel=\"canonical\" href=\"https://tafsirshaikhain.com/en/ayah/61-5.html\">\n<link rel=\"alternate\" hreflang=\"ar\" href=\"https://tafsirshaikhain.com/ayah/61-5.html\">\n<link rel=\"alternate\" hreflang=\"x-default\" href=\"https://tafsirshaikhain.com/ayah/61-5.html\">\n<link rel=\"alternate\" hreflang=\"en\" href=\"https://tafsirshaikhain.com/en/ayah/61-5.html\">\n<link rel=\"alternate\" hreflang=\"ur\" href=\"https://tafsirshaikhain.com/ur/ayah/61-5.html\">\n<link rel=\"alternate\" hreflang=\"id\" href=\"https://tafsirshaikhain.com/id/ayah/61-5.html\">\n<link rel=\"alternate\" hreflang=\"tr\" href=\"https://tafsirshaikhain.com/tr/ayah/61-5.html\">\n<link rel=\"alternate\" hreflang=\"fr\" href=\"https://tafsirshaikhain.com/fr/ayah/61-5.html\">\n<link rel=\"alternate\" hreflang=\"bn\" href=\"https://tafsirshaikhain.com/bn/ayah/61-5.html\">\n<link rel=\"alternate\" hreflang=\"ms\" href=\"https://tafsirshaikhain.com/ms/ayah/61-5.html\">\n<link rel=\"alternate\" hreflang=\"fa\" href=\"https://tafsirshaikhain.com/fa/ayah/61-5.html\">\n<link rel=\"alternate\" hreflang=\"ru\" href=\"https://tafsirshaikhain.com/ru/ayah/61-5.html\">\n<link rel=\"alternate\" hreflang=\"sw\" href=\"https://tafsirshaikhain.com/sw/ayah/61-5.html\">\n<link rel=\"alternate\" hreflang=\"ha\" href=\"https://tafsirshaikhain.com/ha/ayah/61-5.html\">\n<link rel=\"alternate\" hreflang=\"es\" href=\"https://tafsirshaikhain.com/es/ayah/61-5.html\">\n<link rel=\"alternate\" hreflang=\"de\" href=\"https://tafsirshaikhain.com/de/ayah/61-5.html\">\n<link rel=\"alternate\" hreflang=\"zh\" href=\"https://tafsirshaikhain.com/zh/ayah/61-5.html\">\n<meta property=\"og:title\" content=\"Tafsir of As-Saff 61:5 — by Ibn Taymiyyah and Ibn al-Qayyim\">\n<meta property=\"og:description\" content=\"And [mention, O Muḥammad], when Moses said to his people, &quot;O my people, why do you harm me while you certainly know that I am the messenger of Allāh to you\">\n<meta name=\"theme-color\" content=\"#1f4d3a\">\n<meta property=\"og:image\" content=\"https://tafsirshaikhain.com/og.png\">\n<meta name=\"twitter:card\" content=\"summary_large_image\">\n<script type=\"application/ld+json\">{\"@context\": \"https://schema.org\", \"@type\": \"BreadcrumbList\", \"itemListElement\": [{\"@type\": \"ListItem\", \"position\": 1, \"name\": \"Home\", \"item\": \"https://tafsirshaikhain.com/en/\"}, {\"@type\": \"ListItem\", \"position\": 2, \"name\": \"Surah As-Saff\", \"item\": \"https://tafsirshaikhain.com/en/surah/61.html\"}, {\"@type\": \"ListItem\", \"position\": 3, \"name\": \"Verse 5\", \"item\": \"https://tafsirshaikhain.com/en/ayah/61-5.html\"}]}</script>\n<link rel=\"icon\" href=\"/icon.svg\" type=\"image/svg+xml\">\n<link rel=\"preconnect\" href=\"https://fonts.googleapis.com\">\n<link rel=\"stylesheet\" href=\"https://fonts.googleapis.com/css2?family=Amiri+Quran&family=Amiri:wght@400;700&family=Noto+Naskh+Arabic:wght@400;600&display=swap\">\n<link rel=\"stylesheet\" href=\"/theme.css\">\n<style>body{font-family:system-ui,\"Segoe UI\",sans-serif;color:var(--ink);padding:20px 16px 48px;line-height:1.6}.tr{font-size:17px;line-height:1.8;margin:0}.cr{font-size:12px;color:var(--muted)}.ar{direction:rtl;text-align:right}</style>\n</head>\n<body>\n<main class=\"sp\"><nav class=\"crumbs\"><a href=\"/en/\">Home</a> › <a href=\"/en/surah/61.html\">Surah As-Saff</a> › Verse 5</nav><h1>Tafsir of Surah As-Saff 61:5</h1><p class=\"vt ar\" lang=\"ar\">﴿وَإِذْ قَالَ مُوسَىٰ لِقَوْمِهِ يَا قَوْمِ لِمَ تُؤْذُونَنِي وَقَد تَّعْلَمُونَ أَنِّي رَسُولُ اللَّهِ إِلَيْكُمْ فَلَمَّا زَاغُوا أَزَاغَ اللَّهُ قُلُوبَهُمْ وَاللَّهُ لَا يَهْدِي الْقَوْمَ الْفَاسِقِينَ﴾</p><section><h3>Translation of the meaning</h3><p class=\"tr\">And [mention, O Muḥammad], when Moses said to his people, &quot;O my people, why do you harm me while you certainly know that I am the messenger of Allāh to you?&quot; And when they deviated, Allāh caused their hearts to deviate. And Allāh does not guide the defiantly disobedient people.</p><span class=\"cr\" dir=\"ltr\">English Translation - Noor International Center — v1.1.2 · QuranEnc.com</span></section><p class=\"cr\">The words of the two imams are given in their original Arabic, verbatim, with references.</p><section><h2>Imam Ibn al-Qayyim</h2><blockquote class=\"ar\" lang=\"ar\">فمن لم يستجب لله ورسوله إذا دعاه حال بينه وبين قلبه وإرادته، فلا يمكنه الاستجابة بعد ذلك،<cite>«زاد المعاد في هدي خير العباد» 3/503</cite></blockquote></section><a class=\"btn pri open\" href=\"/tafsir.html?lang=en#s61a5\">Open in the interactive tafsir (full texts)</a><div class=\"pn\"><a href=\"/en/ayah/61-3.html\">Previous verse (61:3)</a><a href=\"/en/ayah/61-12.html\">Next verse (61:12)</a></div></main><footer class=\"site-foot\"><span>Tafsir al-Shaykhayn · <a href=\"/en/\">Home</a> · <a href=\"/about.html\">About the project</a> · <a href=\"/privacy.html\">Privacy &amp; terms</a></span><a href=\"https://doersadv.com\" rel=\"noopener\" dir=\"ltr\">Developed by Doers</a></footer>\n</body>\n</html>\n","ayah/61-12.html":"<!doctype html>\n<html lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\">\n<head>\n<meta charset=\"utf-8\">\n<meta name=\"viewport\" content=\"width=device-width, initial-scale=1\">\n<title>Tafsir of As-Saff 61:12 — by Ibn Taymiyyah and Ibn al-Qayyim</title>\n<meta name=\"description\" content=\"He will forgive for you your sins and admit you to gardens beneath which rivers flow and pleasant dwellings in gardens of perpetual residence. That is the \">\n<link rel=\"canonical\" href=\"https://tafsirshaikhain.com/en/ayah/61-12.html\">\n<link rel=\"alternate\" hreflang=\"ar\" href=\"https://tafsirshaikhain.com/ayah/61-12.html\">\n<link rel=\"alternate\" hreflang=\"x-default\" href=\"https://tafsirshaikhain.com/ayah/61-12.html\">\n<link rel=\"alternate\" hreflang=\"en\" href=\"https://tafsirshaikhain.com/en/ayah/61-12.html\">\n<link rel=\"alternate\" hreflang=\"ur\" href=\"https://tafsirshaikhain.com/ur/ayah/61-12.html\">\n<link rel=\"alternate\" hreflang=\"id\" href=\"https://tafsirshaikhain.com/id/ayah/61-12.html\">\n<link rel=\"alternate\" hreflang=\"tr\" href=\"https://tafsirshaikhain.com/tr/ayah/61-12.html\">\n<link rel=\"alternate\" hreflang=\"fr\" href=\"https://tafsirshaikhain.com/fr/ayah/61-12.html\">\n<link rel=\"alternate\" hreflang=\"bn\" href=\"https://tafsirshaikhain.com/bn/ayah/61-12.html\">\n<link rel=\"alternate\" hreflang=\"ms\" href=\"https://tafsirshaikhain.com/ms/ayah/61-12.html\">\n<link rel=\"alternate\" hreflang=\"fa\" href=\"https://tafsirshaikhain.com/fa/ayah/61-12.html\">\n<link rel=\"alternate\" hreflang=\"ru\" href=\"https://tafsirshaikhain.com/ru/ayah/61-12.html\">\n<link rel=\"alternate\" hreflang=\"sw\" href=\"https://tafsirshaikhain.com/sw/ayah/61-12.html\">\n<link rel=\"alternate\" hreflang=\"ha\" href=\"https://tafsirshaikhain.com/ha/ayah/61-12.html\">\n<link rel=\"alternate\" hreflang=\"es\" href=\"https://tafsirshaikhain.com/es/ayah/61-12.html\">\n<link rel=\"alternate\" hreflang=\"de\" href=\"https://tafsirshaikhain.com/de/ayah/61-12.html\">\n<link rel=\"alternate\" hreflang=\"zh\" href=\"https://tafsirshaikhain.com/zh/ayah/61-12.html\">\n<meta property=\"og:title\" content=\"Tafsir of As-Saff 61:12 — by Ibn Taymiyyah and Ibn al-Qayyim\">\n<meta property=\"og:description\" content=\"He will forgive for you your sins and admit you to gardens beneath which rivers flow and pleasant dwellings in gardens of perpetual residence. That is the \">\n<meta name=\"theme-color\" content=\"#1f4d3a\">\n<meta property=\"og:image\" content=\"https://tafsirshaikhain.com/og.png\">\n<meta name=\"twitter:card\" content=\"summary_large_image\">\n<script type=\"application/ld+json\">{\"@context\": \"https://schema.org\", \"@type\": \"BreadcrumbList\", \"itemListElement\": [{\"@type\": \"ListItem\", \"position\": 1, \"name\": \"Home\", \"item\": \"https://tafsirshaikhain.com/en/\"}, {\"@type\": \"ListItem\", \"position\": 2, \"name\": \"Surah As-Saff\", \"item\": \"https://tafsirshaikhain.com/en/surah/61.html\"}, {\"@type\": \"ListItem\", \"position\": 3, \"name\": \"Verse 12\", \"item\": \"https://tafsirshaikhain.com/en/ayah/61-12.html\"}]}</script>\n<link rel=\"icon\" href=\"/icon.svg\" type=\"image/svg+xml\">\n<link rel=\"preconnect\" href=\"https://fonts.googleapis.com\">\n<link rel=\"stylesheet\" href=\"https://fonts.googleapis.com/css2?family=Amiri+Quran&family=Amiri:wght@400;700&family=Noto+Naskh+Arabic:wght@400;600&display=swap\">\n<link rel=\"stylesheet\" href=\"/theme.css\">\n<style>body{font-family:system-ui,\"Segoe UI\",sans-serif;color:var(--ink);padding:20px 16px 48px;line-height:1.6}.tr{font-size:17px;line-height:1.8;margin:0}.cr{font-size:12px;color:var(--muted)}.ar{direction:rtl;text-align:right}</style>\n</head>\n<body>\n<main class=\"sp\"><nav class=\"crumbs\"><a href=\"/en/\">Home</a> › <a href=\"/en/surah/61.html\">Surah As-Saff</a> › Verse 12</nav><h1>Tafsir of Surah As-Saff 61:12</h1><p class=\"vt ar\" lang=\"ar\">﴿يَغْفِرْ لَكُمْ ذُنُوبَكُمْ وَيُدْخِلْكُمْ جَنَّاتٍ تَجْرِي مِن تَحْتِهَا الْأَنْهَارُ وَمَسَاكِنَ طَيِّبَةً فِي جَنَّاتِ عَدْنٍ ذَٰلِكَ الْفَوْزُ الْعَظِيمُ﴾</p><section><h3>Translation of the meaning</h3><p class=\"tr\">He will forgive for you your sins and admit you to gardens beneath which rivers flow and pleasant dwellings in gardens of perpetual residence. That is the great attainment.</p><span class=\"cr\" dir=\"ltr\">English Translation - Noor International Center — v1.1.2 · QuranEnc.com</span></section><p class=\"cr\">The words of the two imams are given in their original Arabic, verbatim, with references.</p><section><h2>Shaykh al-Islam Ibn Taymiyyah</h2><blockquote class=\"ar\" lang=\"ar\">فبين ما فيه من دفع مفسدة الذنوب ومن حصول مصلحة الرحمة بالجنة<cite>«مجموع الفتاوى» 20/194</cite></blockquote></section><a class=\"btn pri open\" href=\"/tafsir.html?lang=en#s61a12\">Open in the interactive tafsir (full texts)</a><div class=\"pn\"><a href=\"/en/ayah/61-5.html\">Previous verse (61:5)</a><a href=\"/en/ayah/61-13.html\">Next verse (61:13)</a></div></main><footer class=\"site-foot\"><span>Tafsir al-Shaykhayn · <a href=\"/en/\">Home</a> · <a href=\"/about.html\">About the project</a> · <a href=\"/privacy.html\">Privacy &amp; terms</a></span><a href=\"https://doersadv.com\" rel=\"noopener\" dir=\"ltr\">Developed by Doers</a></footer>\n</body>\n</html>\n","ayah/61-13.html":"<!doctype html>\n<html lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\">\n<head>\n<meta charset=\"utf-8\">\n<meta name=\"viewport\" content=\"width=device-width, initial-scale=1\">\n<title>Tafsir of As-Saff 61:13 — by Ibn Taymiyyah and Ibn al-Qayyim</title>\n<meta name=\"description\" content=\"And [you will obtain] another [favor] that you love - victory from Allāh and an imminent conquest; and give goo